      "beat_id": "BDEFS",
      "act": "terms",
      "lane": "bookend",
      "proof_gate": "CARD",
      "narration_text": "Six terms. Slash projects: persistent shared storage on Explorer, up to 35 terabytes free, right place for research data and shared pipelines, not slash scratch. The project command: terminal tool that lets PIs and delegates manage membership directly, no ticket. PI: project owner, full control over roles, email, and TTL. Delegate: trusted lab member promoted by the PI, can add and remove members and guests. T T L, time to live: administrative marker, not a countdown — Research Computing emails the PI when it expires, data untouched. And IB constraint: InfiniBand network fabric required by the project command, which is why you land on a compute node before running anything.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 44.0,
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
